## Downloads and Exports

The app maps native WebKit downloads to an `NSSavePanel`.

For single-file app exports that use `a[download]` with `blob:` or `data:` URLs, the generated app installs a narrow save-file bridge. It handles normal clicks and common programmatic `anchor.click()` exports, reads the generated bytes in the WebView, and asks macOS where to save them. It does not expose general native filesystem access to JavaScript.

Broader browser behaviors, multi-file asset discovery, and native open dialogs may need app-specific native helpers.

## Signing and Notarization

Unsigned local builds are useful for personal use and testing.

For distribution to other Macs, configure Apple Developer code signing and notarization.
